{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wqb3z6smyfvppd2ikutool45o5irhthrgkrf25vkj3vkh2dhvrjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Xb7rsqsjhypvwHErFLoBCy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-KcJ46a/translation/CONFIGS.md","content":"# CONFIGS.md — configuration-surface table (Phase A/B)\n\nDerived mechanically from the branches `c_src/cJSON.c` actually takes on\n*valid* input. Axes were enumerated from the public header\n(`c_src/cJSON.h`) plus every `if` / `switch` / `#ifdef` the C code evaluates on a\nruntime option or on the shape of the data.\n\n## Axes the C code branches on\n\n### A. Allocator configuration (`cJSON_InitHooks`, lines 176–205)\nSelects `global_hooks.{allocate,deallocate,reallocate}` and therefore which of\ntwo *completely different* buffer-growth paths `ensure` (502–530) and `print`\n(1227–1248) take:\n\n| id | `cJSON_InitHooks` argument | resulting `reallocate` | growth path |\n|----|-----------------------------|------------------------|-------------|\n| A0 | never called / `NULL` (reset) | `realloc` | `ensure`: 505 `reallocate`; `print`: 1229 `reallocate` |\n| A1 | `{malloc_fn = libc malloc, free_fn = libc free}` | `realloc` (both equal the libc originals, 201) | same as A0 |\n| A2 | `{malloc_fn = custom, free_fn = custom}` | `NULL` | `ensure`: 518 `allocate` + `memcpy` + `deallocate`; `print`: 1237 `allocate` + `memcpy` (`cjson_min` clamp) |\n| A3 | `{malloc_fn = custom, free_fn = NULL}` | `NULL` (`deallocate` = libc `free`, `allocate` ≠ `malloc`) | manual path |\n| A4 | `{malloc_fn = NULL, free_fn = custom}` | `NULL` | manual path |\n| A5 | `{malloc_fn = NULL, free_fn = NULL}` | `realloc` | same as A0 |\n\n### B. Print entry point × `format` flag\n`cJSON_Print` (format=1) · `cJSON_PrintUnformatted` (format=0) ·\n`cJSON_PrintBuffered(prebuffer, fmt)` (`noalloc=0`, caller-chosen initial size) ·\n`cJSON_PrintPreallocated(buf, length, format)` (`noalloc=1`, **no** growth at all).\n`format` gates 9 distinct branches: `print_array` 1589/1596, `print_object`\n1749/1758/1766/1795/1809/1820/1830/1835.\n\n### C. Parse entry point × options\n`cJSON_Parse` · `cJSON_ParseWithLength(len)` · `cJSON_ParseWithOpts(end, rnt)` ·\n`cJSON_ParseWithLengthOpts(len, end, rnt)`.\nOptions: `return_parse_end` NULL/non-NULL (1149), `require_null_terminated`\n0/non-0 (1141), and `buffer_length` exact / longer / shorter than `strlen+1`\n(`can_read`/`can_access_at_index`, 266–268).\n\n### D. Value type (`print_value` switch on `type & 0xFF`, 1394; `parse_value`, 1339–1379)\n`cJSON_NULL` · `cJSON_False` · `cJSON_True` · `cJSON_Number` · `cJSON_Raw` ·\n`cJSON_String` · `cJSON_Array` · `cJSON_Object`, each optionally OR-ed with\n`cJSON_IsReference` (256) and/or `cJSON_StringIsConst` (512) — both of which are\nmasked out of the switch but change `cJSON_Delete` (226/230/235),\n`cJSON_Duplicate` (2760/2773), `add_item_to_object` (2060), `replace_item_in_object`\n(2387) and `cJSON_SetValuestring` (403).\n\n### E. Number shape (`print_number`, 558–625; `parse_number`, 274–375)\n`isnan`/`isinf` → `\"null\"` · `d == (double)valueint` → `\"%d\"` ·\n`\"%1.15g\"` round-trips (`sscanf` + `compare_double`) · otherwise `\"%1.17g\"`.\nSaturation boundaries `>= INT_MAX`, `<= (double)INT_MIN`, else `(int)d`.\nLocale decimal point substitution (`get_decimal_point`, `ENABLE_LOCALES`).\n\n### F. String shape (`print_string_ptr` 916–1035; `parse_string` 786–913)\n`NULL` → `\"\"` · no escapes needed (`memcpy` fast path, 976) · one-char escapes\n`\" \\ \\b \\f \\n \\r \\t` · bytes `< 32` → `\\u00xx` (5 extra chars) · bytes `> 127`\ncopied verbatim · parse-side escapes `\\b \\f \\n \\r \\t \\\" \\\\ \\/` and `\\uXXXX`\n(1/2/3/4-byte UTF-8, surrogate pairs).\n\n### G. Container shape\n0 / 1 / many children; nesting depth 1 … 999 (limit 1000); arrays vs objects vs\nmixed; `child->prev` circular back-pointer maintenance\n(`add_item_to_array` 1992–2007, `parse_array` 1536, `cJSON_Create*Array` 2606).\n\n### H. Lookup / mutation index & key\n`case_sensitive` 0/1 (`get_object_item`, 1913); index 0 / middle / last;\nkey present / duplicate keys / differing case.\n\n### I. `cJSON_Duplicate` `recurse` 0/1 (2780) and `cJSON_Compare` `case_sensitive` 0/1.\n\n### J. `cJSON_Minify` token classes (2887–2917)\nwhitespace ` \\t\\r\\n` · `//` line comment · `/* */` block comment · lone `/` ·\nstring literal with escaped quotes (`minify_string`, 2854–2874) · other bytes.\n\n---\n\n## Configuration rows (cross-product, pruned to what the C distinguishes)\n\nEvery row is exercised with **many randomized inputs** from a fixed-seed PRNG\n(`harness::Rng`) and asserted byte-for-byte / field-for-field between the C and\nthe Rust `.so`.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `cJSON_Version` | no input | [x] |\n| 2 | `cJSON_malloc` / `cJSON_free` | sizes 0, 1, 8, 4096, 1 MiB (A0) | [x] |\n| 3 | `cJSON_CreateNull/True/False` | — (check `type`, all fields zero) | [x] |\n| 4 | `cJSON_CreateBool` | `boolean` = 0, 1, and out-of-range ints 2/-1/`INT_MIN` | [x] |\n| 5 | `cJSON_CreateNumber` | random `json_f64()`: 0, -0, ±small ints, `INT_MAX`/`INT_MIN` ± ε, huge, denormal, ±inf, NaN → check `type`/`valueint`/`valuedouble` bits | [x] |\n| 6 | `cJSON_CreateString` | empty / ASCII / all one-char-escape bytes / bytes 1..31 / high bytes 128..255 / long | [x] |\n| 7 | `cJSON_CreateRaw` | same shapes as row 6 | [x] |\n| 8 | `cJSON_CreateStringReference` | `type == String\\|IsReference`, `valuestring` aliases the caller's buffer | [x] |\n| 9 | `cJSON_CreateArray` / `cJSON_CreateObject` | empty containers | [x] |\n| 10 | `cJSON_CreateObjectReference` / `cJSON_CreateArrayReference` | non-NULL child; `type` has `IsReference`; `cJSON_Delete` must not free the child | [x] |\n| 11 | `cJSON_CreateIntArray` | `count` = 0, 1, 2, 3, 17, 256 × random `int` values incl. `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` | [x] |\n| 12 | `cJSON_CreateFloatArray` | `count` = 0, 1, many × random `f32` incl. ±inf/NaN/denormal (note the `float→double` widening) | [x] |\n| 13 | `cJSON_CreateDoubleArray` | `count` = 0, 1, many × random `f64` from `json_f64()` | [x] |\n| 14 | `cJSON_CreateStringArray` | `count` = 0, 1, many × strings from row 6's pool | [x] |\n| 15 | `cJSON_GetArraySize` / `cJSON_GetArrayItem` | arrays of size 0/1/5/64, index 0 / middle / last / `size` / `size+1` | [x] |\n| 16 | `cJSON_GetObjectItem` (case-insensitive) | key exact / different case / mixed case / duplicate keys / absent | [x] |\n| 17 | `cJSON_GetObjectItemCaseSensitive` | same keys as row 16 | [x] |\n| 18 | `cJSON_HasObjectItem` | same keys as row 16 | [x] |\n| 19 | `cJSON_GetStringValue` / `cJSON_GetNumberValue` | one item of each of the 9 types | [x] |\n| 20 | all 10 `cJSON_Is*` predicates | one item of each of the 9 types, ± `IsReference`, ± `StringIsConst`, plus raw `type` values 0/3/0x0A/0xFF/256/512 | [x] |\n| 21 | `cJSON_AddItemToArray` | append into empty / 1-element / n-element array; append the same item twice | [x] |\n| 22 | `cJSON_AddItemToObject` | keys: empty, ASCII, needing escapes, duplicate; item already having a `string` (freed) | [x] |\n| 23 | `cJSON_AddItemToObjectCS` | constant key ⇒ `type \\|= StringIsConst`; then `cJSON_Delete` must not free the key | [x] |\n| 24 | `cJSON_AddItemReferenceToArray` / `…ToObject` | referencing a live subtree; printing and deleting the parent | [x] |\n| 25 | `cJSON_AddNull/True/False/Bool/Number/String/Raw/Object/ArrayToObject` | all 9 helpers on a fresh object, randomized names/values | [x] |\n| 26 | `cJSON_Print` (A0, format=1) | every type from row 20 and randomized nested trees | [x] |\n| 27 | `cJSON_PrintUnformatted` (A0, format=0) | same trees as row 26 | [x] |\n| 28 | `cJSON_PrintBuffered` (A0, fmt=1) | `prebuffer` = 0, 1, 2, 8, 255, 256, 257, 1024, 65536 (crosses the `ensure` grow/`INT_MAX/2` logic) | [x] |\n| 29 | `cJSON_PrintBuffered` (A0, fmt=0) | same prebuffer sweep | [x] |\n| 30 | `cJSON_PrintPreallocated` (format=1) | `length` = exact, exact-1, exact+1, exact+5, 0, 1 — must agree on both the return value **and** the bytes written into the buffer | [x] |\n| 31 | `cJSON_PrintPreallocated` (format=0) | same length sweep | [x] |\n| 32 | `print_number` via all 4 print entry points | numbers that take each of the 4 formatting branches: NaN/±inf → `null`; integral == `valueint`; 15-significant-digit round-trip; 17-digit fallback; plus `valueint` desynchronised from `valuedouble` via a direct field write | [x] |\n| 33 | `print_string_ptr` via all 4 print entry points | `NULL` `valuestring`; no-escape fast path; every one-char escape; every byte 1..31; bytes 128..255; strings whose escape count changes the `output_length` arithmetic | [x] |\n| 34 | `print_object` (format=1) nesting | depth 1..8 objects/arrays → the `depth` indentation loops (1774, 1838) | [x] |\n| 35 | `cJSON_Parse` | valid JSON of every type, randomized generated documents | [x] |\n| 36 | `cJSON_ParseWithLength` | `len` = `strlen+1` (canonical), `strlen` (no NUL visible), `strlen+2`, and `len` shorter than the document | [x] |\n| 37 | `cJSON_ParseWithOpts(end = &p, rnt = 0)` | valid JSON with trailing garbage — `*end` offset compared | [x] |\n| 38 | `cJSON_ParseWithOpts(end = &p, rnt = 1)` | valid JSON, exact / with trailing whitespace / with trailing garbage | [x] |\n| 39 | `cJSON_ParseWithOpts(end = NULL, rnt = 1)` | same inputs, `return_parse_end` omitted | [x] |\n| 40 | `cJSON_ParseWithLengthOpts(len, end, rnt)` | full 2×2×(4 length variants) cross-product | [x] |\n| 41 | parse: leading UTF-8 BOM (`skip_utf8_bom`, 1085) | `\"\\xEF\\xBB\\xBF\" + doc`, and a BOM shorter than 4 readable bytes | [x] |\n| 42 | parse: leading/interior/trailing whitespace (`buffer_skip_whitespace`, 1064) | all bytes `<= 32` as separators, incl. `\\0`-adjacent edge where `offset == length` | [x] |\n| 43 | parse: numbers | `0`, `-0`, integers, `1e309` (→inf), `-1e309`, `1e-400` (→0), 15-digit, 17-digit, `INT_MAX`/`INT_MIN` boundaries, leading zeros, `1.`, `.5`-style rejects (see ERRORS) | [x] |\n| 44 | parse: strings | every escape form, `\\u` BMP, `\\u` surrogate pairs (1/2/3/4-byte UTF-8 output), raw high bytes, empty string, embedded NUL via `\u0000` | [x] |\n| 45 | parse: arrays | `[]`, `[1]`, `[1,2,…]`, whitespace variants, nested to depth 999 | [x] |\n| 46 | parse: objects | `{}`, one key, many keys, duplicate keys, nested to depth 999, whitespace variants | [x] |\n| 47 | parse → print round-trip | parse each generated document, then print with all 4 entry points × `format` and compare | [x] |\n| 48 | `cJSON_GetErrorPtr` | after a successful parse, after each failing parse variant, after `cJSON_ParseWithOpts(NULL, …)` — compared as an **offset** into the input | [x] |\n| 49 | `cJSON_Minify` | whitespace only, `//` comment (with/without trailing newline), `/* */` comment (unterminated), lone `/`, strings containing `\\\"`, `\\\\`, `//`, `/*`, and mixtures; buffer contents after the call compared byte-for-byte over the whole original length | [x] |\n| 50 | `cJSON_Duplicate(recurse = 0)` | every type, ± `IsReference`, ± `StringIsConst`, with/without children | [x] |\n| 51 | `cJSON_Duplicate(recurse = 1)` | nested trees to depth 8, arrays/objects/mixed, `StringIsConst` keys | [x] |\n| 52 | `cJSON_Compare(case_sensitive = 0)` | equal / unequal pairs of every type; objects with keys differing only in case; different orders; subsets | [x] |\n| 53 | `cJSON_Compare(case_sensitive = 1)` | same pairs as row 52 | [x] |\n| 54 | `cJSON_DetachItemViaPointer` | detach first / middle / last / only child of an array and of an object; then re-print the parent and the detached item | [x] |\n| 55 | `cJSON_DetachItemFromArray` | index 0 / middle / last on sizes 1..6 | [x] |\n| 56 | `cJSON_DetachItemFromObject` / `…CaseSensitive` | key present (exact & other case) at first / middle 